# ==============================================================================
# MANOVA + MAHALANOBIS DISTANCE IN PC1 × PC2 SPACE
# ==============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE
#
# Quantify the multivariate separation between compound centroids shown
# in the PCA figure.
#
# IMPORTANT:
#
# Only PC1 and PC2 are used because the target distances correspond to
# the centroid positions displayed in the two-dimensional PCA plots.
#
# Analyses are performed independently for each binding site:
#
#   BZD
#   BB
#   GABA
#
#
# ANALYSES
#
# 1. Omnibus MANOVA:
#
#       cbind(PC1, PC2) ~ compound
#
#    Pillai's trace is used as the primary statistic.
#
#
# 2. Pairwise MANOVA:
#
#    Every unique pair of compounds within each binding site.
#
#    P values are corrected using Benjamini-Hochberg FDR.
#
#
# 3. Mahalanobis distance:
#
#    Calculated between compound centroids in the PC1 × PC2 plane.
#
#    D² = (μ1 - μ2)' S_pooled^-1 (μ1 - μ2)
#
#    D = sqrt(D²)
#
#
# 4. Box's M:
#
#    Diagnostic test for equality of covariance matrices.
#
#
# 5. Outputs:
#
#    - Excel workbook
#    - Mahalanobis distance matrices
#    - Mahalanobis heatmaps
#    - Group centroids
#    - Omnibus MANOVA
#    - Pairwise MANOVA + BH-FDR
#
# ==============================================================================



